__song__ 0 9 0 4 0 1 2 3
__song__ 1 8 0 4 4 5 6 7
__song__ 2 10 0 4 8 9 10 11
__text__ en
char.rei	Rei
title.name	LAST TRAIN\nHOME
title.sub	a NEVEL-98 demo / endings {1} of 3
hud.command	COMMAND
hud.sat	SAT
hud.sun	SUN
start.date	December 31st, 1994. Eight minutes to midnight.
start.board	The departure board flickers over the empty platform.
start.missed	The last train for Shin-Kawa left four minutes ago. I could have caught it. I watched its lights disappear instead.
start.pager	My pager buzzes. {c:8}COME HOME. I KEPT YOUR SEAT.{/c} My sister.
start.pager2	In August I promised I'd be home for Dad's memorial. I didn't go.
start.pager3	When she called, I told her to stop waiting for me. That I wasn't coming back.
start.pager4	She has paged me every night since. I've never called back.
menu.look	Look around
menu.board	Read board
menu.drink	Buy a drink
menu.sit	Sit down
look.1	Rain drums on the roof. Across the river the city is still awake, window by window.
look.2	Someone has carved into the bench: {c:8}R. 1989{/c}, {c:8}R. 1990{/c}, {c:8}R. 1991{/c}... one line for every year, up to this one.
board.1	Every line reads the same: {c:7}SERVICE ENDED{/c}.
board.2	Every line except the last one, which reads {c:8}00:00  HOME{/c}.{w:0.8} ...That can't be right.
drink.1	The machine sells something called {c:8}MELON SODA ROYALE{/c}. The can has a little crown on it.
drink.2	I buy two. One for me, one out of habit: my sister always stole half of mine.
drink.again	I already have two cans. That feels like enough melon for one night.
start.sit	I sit down. The bench is cold enough to bite through my coat.
start.chime	Three notes echo across the platform: the departure chime. No train is coming.
rei.hi1	Ehehe! You missed it too?
rei.hi2	Don't make that face. Missing the last train of the year is practically a tradition.
c.who	"Who are you?"
c.letgo	"I didn't miss it. I let it go."
rei.who	Rei. Just Rei. I come here every New Year's Eve, so technically this is my bench.
rei.who2	But I'll share. I'm generous like that.
rei.letgo	...Oh. That's different.
rei.letgo2	Letting something go on purpose is the hardest way to lose it.
p.waiting	"Are you waiting for someone?"
rei.wait1	Mmh... good question.
rei.wait2	Maybe!
p.maybe	"What do you mean, maybe?"
rei.wait3	It's strange. Every year I come here, I get the feeling I forgot something important.
rei.wait4	But it's probably just the cold! Ehehe!
start.carving	I think of the letters carved into the bench. {c:8}R.{/c} Every year, up to this one.
rei.soda	Wait. Is that {c:8}MELON SODA ROYALE{/c}?! Nobody ever buys that one. It's the best one!
start.soda	I hand her the second can. It feels right, giving away the half somebody used to steal.
start.city	She watches the city across the river as if it were a show put on just for her.
rei.city	I like the city at night. Everyone's busy with their own lives, so nobody's watching you.
rei.city2	You can just... be yourself. Even if you're not completely sure who that is.
start.pager5	The pager buzzes again. {c:8}I KEPT YOUR SEAT.{/c}
rei.pager	Someone really wants you to come home.
c.tell	Tell her about your sister
c.dodge	Change the subject
p.tell	"I told my sister to stop waiting for me."
rei.tell1	And did she?
p.tell2	"...She kept my seat."
rei.tell2	Then she's still waiting, silly. That's the good news!
rei.dodge	Okay. You don't have to tell me.
rei.dodge2	...I'm the same, you know.
rei.pager2	It's going to be fine, you know. Whatever it is. It's always fine in the end!
c.thanks	"Thanks."
c.ask	"And you? Are you okay?"
rei.thanks	Anytime. Cheering up strangers is my second job.
rei.ask1	Me?
rei.ask2	...Nobody's asked me that in a long time.
rei.ask3	I'm fine! Really! Everything's fine.
start.ask4	She says it too fast, and her voice shakes a little. Like a line rehearsed in front of a mirror.
c.pretend	"You don't have to pretend with me."
c.song	"Then let's listen to another song."
c.gohome	"You should go home too."
rei.pretend	...Is it that obvious?
start.pretend	For a moment she stops smiling. It makes her look younger, not older.
rei.song	Ehehe. You're learning fast.
rei.gohome	Maybe I don't have one. ...Kidding! Kidding.
start.radio	She pulls a small, scratched radio out of her coat.
rei.radio	Want to hear something strange? This station only plays songs from next year.
start.radio2	Before the music starts, the speaker gives three notes. The same chime as the platform.
start.song	Then a melody. I've never heard it, and I know every word.
rei.best	Do you know the best thing about this radio?
p.future	"That it plays music from the future?"
rei.best2	No, silly! Every time I switch it on, there's something I haven't heard yet.
rei.best3	It means that somewhere, there's still a tomorrow.
c.notknow	"What if I don't want to know what happens tomorrow?"
c.foryou	"Is there one for you, too?"
rei.notknow	Then we just listen to this song. Until the end.
rei.foryou	...I hope so. I really do.
rei.stop	Do you ever want to stop time? Not forever... just for a little while.
q.midnight	It's almost midnight.
c.stay	Stay and listen
c.walk	Walk home in the rain
street.1	I leave her there. Someone has to be sensible tonight.
street.2	The avenue is a river of reflections. Taxis hiss past without slowing down.
street.3	A truck roars by close enough to rattle the windows.
street.4	Then, faintly, from the direction of the station: a train horn.
street.5	There are no trains at midnight. Not on this line.
c.runback	Run back
c.keep	Keep walking
street.6	I keep walking. At the corner there's a payphone, still warm from the last person who cried into it.
street.7	I dial a number I haven't dialed since August. She picks up on the first ring.
street.8	I say I'm sorry. She says: {c:8}"Your seat's still here, idiot."{/c}
street.9	We talk until the year changes in the middle of a sentence.
street.10	In the morning, walking home, I hear a radio in a shop window. It's the song from the bench. Now everyone knows the words.
street.11	No miracle brought me home. Just a phone call I should have made months ago.
plat.ran	I'm soaked and out of breath. She hasn't moved an inch.
rei.back	Ehehe! I knew you'd come back! I was waiting for you!
rei.stayed	You stayed. Most people don't.
rei.here	You know... I like this place. I'm not sure why, but it feels like home.
plat.train	The clock turns over. Three notes, again. This time, light spills down the tracks.
plat.train2	A train with every window lit pulls in without a sound. The sign on the front says {c:8}HOME{/c}.
plat.board_yes	Just like the last line on the board.
plat.board_no	Above us, the board changes by itself: {c:8}00:00  HOME{/c}.
rei.yours	That's your train.
p.yours	"And yours?"
rei.mine	Mine... hasn't come yet.
p.how	"How do you know?"
rei.just	I just do. Go on, hurry! Your sister's waiting!
plat.decide	She's smiling. But her hands, wrapped around the little radio, are shaking.
c.alone	Get on alone
c.together	"Come with me."
rei.fine	I'm fine. Really! Everything's fine.
plat.fine	She says it the way people close a door.
rei.guilt	Hey. Don't feel guilty for being happy, okay?
plat.alone	The doors close between us. She waves until the platform is just a light in the dark.
plat.morning	When the doors open again, it's morning, and the station is the one near my sister's place.
plat.soda	On the seat beside me there's a can of melon soda. It's still cold.
plat.call	There's a payphone on the platform. I call her. {c:8}"I'm here,"{/c} I say. {c:8}"Keep my seat."{/c}
plat.next	Next New Year's Eve, I'll go back to that bench. And this time I'll ask her how she is. First thing.
rei.angry	You can't just decide what's best for me!
rei.angry2	...Even if you're doing it because you care about me.
plat.mirror	"You did the exact same thing to me, a minute ago."
rei.admit	I've been saying "everything's fine" for so long, I forgot how to say anything else.
rei.home	Maybe home isn't the place you have to go back to. Maybe it's the place where someone's waiting for you.
p.waiting2	"Then someone's waiting for you, too. Right here."
rei.admit2	...Okay. Just to the next stop. Then we'll see.
plat.dawn	We cross the river as the sun comes up.
rei.dawn	Look! A train crossing the river at sunrise! I always wanted to see one from the inside!
plat.newsong	Then the radio plays something new. Rei tilts her head.
rei.newsong	I... don't know this one.
plat.newsong2	For the first time, she doesn't know what comes next. She laughs as if it were the best news in the world.
rei.promise	Promise me something. If one day we forget all of this... we come back here, okay?
plat.call2	At the first stop I find a payphone and call home. Rei holds her can of soda and pretends not to listen.
end.home	HOME
end.next_year	NEXT YEAR
end.long_way	THE LONG WAY
